```
private void checkExtension(BinaryResourceContext context) {
    File file = context.getFile();
    String name = file.getName();
    int dot = name.lastIndexOf('.');
    if (dot <= 0) return;
    String ext = name.substring(dot + 1).toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    if (ext.endsWith("?")) ... 
    if (!ext.equals("png") && !ext.equals("gif") && !ext.equals("webp") && !ext.equals("jpg") && !ext.equals("jpeg")) return;
    byte[] header = new byte[12];
    try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream(file)) {
        int read = fis.read(header);
        if (read < 8) return;
        String actual = detectFormat(header);
        if (actual == null) return;
        if (!actual.equals(ext) && !(actual.equals("jpeg") && (ext.equals("jpg") || ext.equals("jpeg")))) {
            // special case: jpg and jpeg are equivalent
            context.report(ISSUE, Location.create(file), "The icon file extension `." + ext + "` does not match its actual format (" + actual + ")");
        }
    } catch (IOException e) { ... }
}
```

But mapping actual format string to extension: actual "jpeg" vs ext "jpg". We can normalize: expected extension(s) for format. For PNG: png. GIF: gif. WebP: webp. JPEG: jpg, jpeg. If ext not in expected list, report.

